WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.186 --> 00:00:02.809
- The 90's were the best time of all time,

00:00:02.809 --> 00:00:05.294
and the toys rocked, and life was great.

00:00:05.294 --> 00:00:10.294
(upbeat music)

00:00:10.504 --> 00:00:13.095
- [Voiceover] Oh! Hit Clips!

00:00:13.095 --> 00:00:15.394
- It's like 60 seconds of one
song, it's not even a song.

00:00:15.394 --> 00:00:16.323
- What?

00:00:16.323 --> 00:00:18.389
- The only part I remember of that song

00:00:18.389 --> 00:00:20.200
is that 60 seconds of it.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.592
- If Hit Me Baby One More Time
isn't on this, I'm walking.

00:00:22.592 --> 00:00:24.751
- Why did children want
things with one earphone?

00:00:24.751 --> 00:00:27.352
Like, you can't shut your
parents out with one earphone.

00:00:27.352 --> 00:00:29.209
- This feels like something
that Xenon would have,

00:00:29.209 --> 00:00:30.811
because it's like kind of futuristic

00:00:30.811 --> 00:00:32.158
but also extremely shitty.

00:00:32.158 --> 00:00:33.598
- Is there volume? Can
you adjust the volume?

00:00:33.598 --> 00:00:35.107
- It's perfect the way it is.

00:00:35.107 --> 00:00:36.779
- It's amazing where we've
gone in the past 10 years,

00:00:36.779 --> 00:00:39.573
where like this amount of storage can now,

00:00:39.573 --> 00:00:41.446
this is like everything,
where as back then,

00:00:41.446 --> 00:00:44.310
it was the equivalent to
one Oops, I Did It Again.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.625
- Not even!

00:00:45.625 --> 00:00:47.227
- [Voiceover] Tamagotchi's!

00:00:47.227 --> 00:00:49.990
- This was a good idea until you realized

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:52.892
that it could die, and
you had to care for it.

00:00:52.892 --> 00:00:54.541
- I'd feed it in the
morning, go to school.

00:00:54.541 --> 00:00:56.956
I'd race home, and rush to
it and try to save its life

00:00:56.956 --> 00:01:00.137
before it died, and it
always died in my arms.

00:01:00.137 --> 00:01:01.344
- This one's already pooped.

00:01:01.344 --> 00:01:02.352
He's already gone to the corner.

00:01:02.352 --> 00:01:03.151
- We have to clean it.

00:01:03.151 --> 00:01:04.157
- Oh my god, there's three buttons.

00:01:04.157 --> 00:01:05.465
How come I don't know how to use this?

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:06.324
- Push the middle button.

00:01:06.324 --> 00:01:07.003
- Woah!

00:01:07.003 --> 00:01:07.682
- Oh no.

00:01:07.682 --> 00:01:08.900
- I don't know what's happening.

00:01:08.915 --> 00:01:10.330
There's bunch of hearts on the screen.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:11.236
- (laughing) It's just hearts.

00:01:11.236 --> 00:01:12.118
- I think that's good.

00:01:12.118 --> 00:01:13.534
- Tamagotchi just kinda
moves left and right

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.664
with his mouth randomly opening.

00:01:18.034 --> 00:01:20.921
- This is a Skip It,
but it's not a Skip It.

00:01:20.921 --> 00:01:22.663
It's just like, the Walmart Skip It.

00:01:22.663 --> 00:01:24.822
- My favorite ones were
the ones that, like,

00:01:24.822 --> 00:01:26.610
they had a counter on it.

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:28.026
- What do I do?

00:01:28.026 --> 00:01:29.967
- How do you get it going?

00:01:31.505 --> 00:01:32.727
- There you go.

00:01:32.727 --> 00:01:34.148
Ow! F***!

00:01:35.619 --> 00:01:37.082
- Go!

00:01:37.082 --> 00:01:38.329
Keep swinging!

00:01:38.329 --> 00:01:39.590
(laughing) There you go!

00:01:40.496 --> 00:01:42.647
- [Woman in Jacket] This is so
much harder than I remember.

00:01:42.647 --> 00:01:45.180
- I'm not saying I'm
gonna be great at this,

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.430
but I will be great at this.

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:48.531
- Okay let's see it.

00:01:48.531 --> 00:01:49.613
- Okay.

00:01:49.613 --> 00:01:51.493
- Woah!

00:01:51.493 --> 00:01:52.933
- Yeah, Keith! Yeah, Keith!

00:01:52.933 --> 00:01:54.349
There you go!

00:01:54.349 --> 00:01:56.997
- (laughing) How did you do it?

00:01:56.997 --> 00:01:58.552
Alright, here we go.

00:01:58.552 --> 00:02:00.920
Skip It. Skip It.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.824
- See if you can skip up to the top.

00:02:02.824 --> 00:02:05.332
- Were 90's kids just
in really good shape?

00:02:05.332 --> 00:02:06.864
- Gak!

00:02:06.864 --> 00:02:08.350
What does it say? Smelly Gak?

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:09.744
Oh come on!

00:02:09.744 --> 00:02:11.439
- You could order this right out of

00:02:11.439 --> 00:02:12.739
Nickelodeon Magazine, please!

00:02:12.739 --> 00:02:14.503
- What is that smell?

00:02:14.503 --> 00:02:15.827
It's the worst smell!

00:02:15.827 --> 00:02:17.963
- Isn't it crazy that
kids, there's a demand for

00:02:17.963 --> 00:02:20.076
kids to have, like, awful smelling toys?

00:02:20.076 --> 00:02:21.399
- It's feels sweaty.

00:02:21.399 --> 00:02:23.431
- Who can make a (beep) the fastest?

00:02:23.431 --> 00:02:23.977
- Grow up.

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.747
- I'm faking like I have a booger.

00:02:28.438 --> 00:02:30.176
- Ew.

00:02:30.176 --> 00:02:30.797
- Look at it go!

00:02:30.797 --> 00:02:32.826
- You guys, this is amazing!

00:02:32.826 --> 00:02:34.685
Does NASA know about this?

00:02:34.685 --> 00:02:35.079
- Bop It.

00:02:35.079 --> 00:02:36.774
First Generation Bop It, because Bop It

00:02:36.774 --> 00:02:38.608
got way crazy after this.

00:02:38.608 --> 00:02:41.348
- You would just get so dialed in.

00:02:41.348 --> 00:02:43.136
- In the commercials it was
always the coolest thing,

00:02:43.136 --> 00:02:44.970
they were like, always like
bopping it on their hip.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:47.174
(laughing)

00:02:47.174 --> 00:02:48.078
- Ah!

00:02:48.976 --> 00:02:51.309
- No!

00:02:51.309 --> 00:02:52.131
- No!

00:02:52.131 --> 00:02:54.072
- This stressed me out incredibly.

00:02:54.072 --> 00:02:55.605
- [Voiceover] Moon Shoes.

00:02:55.605 --> 00:02:57.810
Kid powered anti-gravity shoes!

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.134
- Do you wanna hold my hands?

00:02:59.134 --> 00:03:01.200
- Not because I need
to, because I want to.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.750
- I think I have to sit down.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.911
Woah!

00:03:04.911 --> 00:03:06.629
- This feels unsafe.

00:03:08.213 --> 00:03:08.750
- [Girl] Oh god.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:09.880
- Okay, okay. That's enough.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:10.901
- [Girl] Okay.

00:03:12.177 --> 00:03:13.432
- What?

00:03:13.432 --> 00:03:16.408
Is that how you play with
them, you just jump around?

00:03:16.408 --> 00:03:18.517
- It's like you're walking on the moon.

00:03:19.409 --> 00:03:21.907
- It's just buckets and bands and velcro.

00:03:21.907 --> 00:03:23.980
- I wanna jump like they
jump in the commercials.

00:03:25.158 --> 00:03:27.389
(laughing)

00:03:27.389 --> 00:03:28.372
- You're supposed to jump.

00:03:28.372 --> 00:03:29.244
- Neil Armstrong, baby.

00:03:29.244 --> 00:03:30.011
- You're supposed to jump.

00:03:30.011 --> 00:03:31.659
- I am not jumping in this thing.

00:03:31.659 --> 00:03:33.099
- I think Moon Shoes should come back.

00:03:33.099 --> 00:03:34.701
- What I like about 90's toys is there's

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:36.512
just a little bit more danger.

00:03:36.512 --> 00:03:39.534
- There's not like a Taylor Swift, 1989

00:03:39.534 --> 00:03:43.094
Hit Clips collection, is there?

00:03:43.094 --> 00:03:44.998
She pulled all her music off of Spotify,

00:03:44.998 --> 00:03:47.397
and put it onto Tiger Hit Clips.

